  abstract = {Multi-dimensional image recovery from incomplete data is a fundamental problem in data processing. Due to its advantage of capturing the correlations between any modes of the multi-dimensional image, i.e., the target tensor, the fully-connected tensor network (FCTN) decomposition has recently shown promising performance on multi-dimensional image recovery. However, FCTN decomposition suffers from computational deficiency, especially for large-scale multi-dimensional images. To address this deficiency, we propose a learnable transform-based FCTN model (termed as T-FCTN), which enjoys the remarkable advantage of FCTN decomposition with cheap computational cost. More concretely, we learn the semi-orthogonal transforms along each mode of the target tensor to project the large-scale tensor X{\textbackslash}documentclass[12pt]\{minimal\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsmath\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{wasysym\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsfonts\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amssymb\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsbsy\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{mathrsfs\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{upgreek\} {\textbackslash}setlength\{{\textbackslash}oddsidemargin\}\{-69pt\} {\textbackslash}begin\{document\}\$\$\{{\textbackslash}mathcal \{X\}\}\$\${\textbackslash}end\{document\}{$\in\backslash$}documentclass[12pt]\{minimal\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsmath\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{wasysym\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsfonts\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amssymb\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsbsy\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{mathrsfs\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{upgreek\} {\textbackslash}setlength\{{\textbackslash}oddsidemargin\}\{-69pt\} {\textbackslash}begin\{document\}\$\${\textbackslash}in \$\${\textbackslash}end\{document\}RI{\texttimes}I{\texttimes}{$\cdots\times$}I{\textbackslash}documentclass[12pt]\{minimal\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsmath\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{wasysym\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsfonts\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amssymb\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsbsy\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{mathrsfs\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{upgreek\} {\textbackslash}setlength\{{\textbackslash}oddsidemargin\}\{-69pt\} {\textbackslash}begin\{document\}\$\$\{{\textbackslash}mathbb \{R\}\}{\textasciicircum}\{I{\textbackslash}times \{I\}{\textbackslash}times \{{\textbackslash}cdots \}{\textbackslash}times \{I\}\}\$\${\textbackslash}end\{document\} into a small-scale essential tensor E{\textbackslash}documentclass[12pt]\{minimal\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsmath\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{wasysym\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsfonts\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amssymb\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsbsy\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{mathrsfs\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{upgreek\} {\textbackslash}setlength\{{\textbackslash}oddsidemargin\}\{-69pt\} {\textbackslash}begin\{document\}\$\$\{{\textbackslash}mathcal \{E\}\}\$\${\textbackslash}end\{document\}{$\in\backslash$}documentclass[12pt]\{minimal\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsmath\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{wasysym\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsfonts\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amssymb\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsbsy\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{mathrsfs\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{upgreek\} {\textbackslash}setlength\{{\textbackslash}oddsidemargin\}\{-69pt\} {\textbackslash}begin\{document\}\$\${\textbackslash}in \$\${\textbackslash}end\{document\}Rr{\texttimes}r{\texttimes}{$\cdots\times$}r{\textbackslash}documentclass[12pt]\{minimal\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsmath\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{wasysym\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsfonts\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amssymb\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{amsbsy\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{mathrsfs\} {\textbackslash}usepackage\{upgreek\} {\textbackslash}setlength\{{\textbackslash}oddsidemargin\}\{-69pt\} {\textbackslash}begin\{document\}\$\$\{{\textbackslash}mathbb \{R\}\}{\textasciicircum}\{r{\textbackslash}times \{r\}{\textbackslash}times \{{\textb